// Q-044 `quillo check` lets `n / 4` through where a builtin takes an int: it is an int only when it divides evenly, so it fails at run time for some n
// mode: check
// open-when: /components\)\s*$/
// fixed-when: divides evenly
// From FEEDBACK4.md (found on 5d2e21e). In the bank's lib/iban.qwe, grouping an account number
// in fours: `range(0, (len(c) + 3) / 4)`. `/` is exact in Quillo: `6 / 3` is the int 2 but
// `7 / 2` is the float 3.5, and `range` takes ints, so it worked for some lengths and stopped
// for others. Fixed by a warning from `quillo check` (branch bank-fixes); `floor(...)` fixes
// the code.

fn groups(s: str) -> list = range(0, (len(s) + 3) / 4)

print(groups("abcdefgh"))
